# 19. Real Project Troubleshooting (BofA)

During the Receiver project, several practical issues were encountered:

### ImagePullBackOff

Cause:

Registry Secret was missing.

Resolution:

- Created required Secret.
- Linked Secret to Service Account.
- Restarted Deployment.

Application deployed successfully.

---

### Deployment Not Created

Cause:

Incorrect Project Name in Jenkins/CD configuration.

Resolution:

Updated project configuration and redeployed.

---

### MQ Certificates

Cause:

Required certificate missing.

Resolution:

Certificate added as Secret.

Deployment succeeded.

---

### Log Directory

Application attempted

```
/logs
```

Result

```
Could not create directory
```

Resolution

Use console logging.

Allow OpenShift and Splunk to manage log collection.

---

### Route Testing

Application verified through

- Secure Route
- Unsecure Route
- Port Forwarding

This helped isolate whether the issue was in the application or the networking layer.

