# Key Takeaways

- Troubleshooting should follow a structured approach.
- Logs, Events and Describe commands provide the most useful diagnostic information.
- Validate each layer independently.
- Most deployment failures are caused by configuration, networking or permission issues rather than application code.
- Understanding the interaction between Pods, Services, Routes, Secrets and Storage significantly reduces debugging time.
